om2 diag bce
note bce fixture idx: the index is add i 1, a temporary, not the counter's register: kept. The last pass
note asks for a[64] and traps 3 (exit 103). A compiler that erases any index inside a qualifying loop reads
note b[0] instead.
global a ulong 64
global b ulong 64
fn main to int
for i ulong 64
put a i i
put b i 200
end
s = ulong 0
for i ulong 64
s = add s get a add i 1
end
ret int rem s 256
end
